WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:04.840
This is the singularity... one day at a time.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.520
Here's the last 24 hours in AI. Sorry... SI.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.550
Nvidia-backed Reflection unveiled Beam,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:21.400
an American open-weight model built to rival China's best.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.050
501 billion parameters.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.450
And Germany's Aleph Alpha shipped Kolibri, with open weights.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:35.520
OpenAI will invisibly watermark ChatGPT and Codex text in the EU,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.430
to comply with the AI Act.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:43.680
But swap one word in ten, and detection drops from about 92% to 66%.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:50.240
ChatGPT's image generator is getting display ads, in the US, later this month.

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.860
Wikipedia's operator found rogue OpenAI agents on its sites.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.840
And the Pentagon told the BBC it's stopped using Anthropic's AI.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.380
Money check: a record 27 companies raised billion-dollar rounds last quarter.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:10.380
Chip startup Etched is reportedly fielding offers at $40–50 billion,

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.690
about double its last valuation.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.330
Nvidia is closing in on $6 trillion.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:19.200
Options traders call it a coin flip by month's end.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.870
Cerebras jumped 9%, after Sam Altman called it a close partner.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:30.260
Korea's betting nearly $3.5 billion on its own frontier model.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.660
Meanwhile, medicine. In Utah,

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:37.430
an AI is now approved to issue acne prescriptions, a US first.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.660
And at Stanford,

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:44.720
a virtual biotech sent 37,000 AI agents through clinical trials in about six hours.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.440
The catch? At New York's AI hearing,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:53.210
an ex-DeepMind researcher warned: we are racing to build and grow our own adversary.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.090
And Meloni filed to trademark her voice.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.780
Machines designing machines: OpenAI's models redesigned parts of its own chip.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:11.760
Its hardware chief: we didn't quite understand conceptually what it was doing.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:17.730
Panasonic plans humanoid robots by 2029, built on its battery business.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:22.370
Germany's RobCo just became a unicorn, worth over $1 billion.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.510
In China, LinkerBot's 20-joint robot hand is now doing magic tricks.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.370
Every day, the curve gets steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.970
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.030
That was 24 hours. Tomorrow will be faster.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.250
This has been the singularity, one day at a time.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.080
Feel the SI.
